All six reverts were applied with an asserted-unique string replacement
(python assert count==1) so no mutation silently no-op'd.
DISCLOSURE (the brief anticipated this): M7 — removing ONLY the SinceStart
skip while leaving the pre-existing `year <= 0` floor intact leaves
TestClampedSchedules_TimelineSkipsAlreadyRunningSources PASSING. The new
timeline guard is therefore defence-in-depth rather than the sole producer of
the behaviour, and the shipped test does not independently mutation-kill that
one line. The behaviour the criterion states (a SinceStart source yields no
"starts" event) IS pinned by the test and confirmed by my direct builder probe,
and the combined mutation the brief prescribed does fail it. Not a criterion
failure; recorded because it is the kind of thing a later refactor of the floor
would silently un-guard.

