Observations (not FAIL)
1. `internal/handlers/whatif/handlers_spending_graph.go:235`
   (`addProjectedSSFundingMarkers`) still gates on `entry.StartMonth < 0` and
   will emit an "X starts" marker at month 0 for an already-claiming projected
   Social Security entry. This is `retirement.ProjectedSSEntries`, derived from
   the claim age, NOT a rollover-clamped IncomeSource, so it is outside the
   enumerated surfaces of the attempt-3 contract and outside the O5 grep's
   scope. Same cosmetic class as the marker rule though; backlog candidate.
2. The new timeline guard is not independently mutation-killed (M7 above) —
   only the combined skip+floor mutation fails the test. If the `year <= 0`
   floor in appendEvent is ever relaxed, that test is the only thing standing
   between the clamped fixture and a "Pension starts" at year 0, and it would
   still pass on the skip alone. A test that pins the SinceStart skip without
   depending on the floor (e.g. asserting on a source at StartMonth 0 with a
   projection whose maxYear permits year 0) would close it.
3. Backlog item "RC3.2/checker-tests: rc3_oracle_test.go:301 bans two ids no
   template renders" still stands in the attempt-3 oracle (the `hx-put=`
   clause is what grades); the shipped handler test does not have that gap —
